cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mmokken: Mokken Scale Analysis in Python"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Diederick
    family-names: Stoel
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # TODO: fill in
    # affiliation: "TODO"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-05-14"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/diederickstoel/mmokken"
abstract: >-
  mmokken is a Python implementation of Mokken Scale Analysis (Mokken,
  1971): a non-parametric item response theory framework for ordinal
  psychometric measurement. The package ports the unidimensional analyses,
  automated item selection procedure (AISP) including the genetic
  algorithm variant, and the standard diagnostic checks (manifest
  monotonicity, restscore, P-matrix, reliability, person-fit) from the R
  `mokken` package (Van der Ark, 2007). Numerical results are validated
  against both the canonical R `mokken` 3.1.2 release (CRAN, 2024) and
  the original MSPWIN 5 program (ProGAMMA, 2003).
keywords:
  - psychometrics
  - mokken
  - item response theory
  - non-parametric
  - scale analysis
  - python
